{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-mobile/pulls/369","id":4738262508,"node_id":"PR_kwDOR1UIZs8AAAABGmwl7A","html_url":"https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-mobile/pull/369","diff_url":"https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-mobile/pull/369.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-mobile/pull/369.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-mobile/issues/369","number":369,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"fix(health): durable sign-out revocation of on-device health consent (split H7 of #317)","user":{"login":"BradleyGleavePortfolio","id":264851314,"node_id":"U_kgDOD8lPcg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/264851314?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio","html_url":"https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BradleyGleavePortfolio/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Tier: T4** (health data, auth/sign-out, account deletion path; max-tier rule). Opened by B-HC8-119 (agent 119). Parent owner: operator (lands with #359-#364 as one, rule 11).\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Tier | T4 |\n| Why | Local Health Connect / Apple Health consent must not survive sign-out (Sol B-362-8, B-362-9 on #362 @ `261e7d4c`; Sol B-369-1 on this PR @ `35717bfe`) |\n| T4 trigger scan | health data consent, sign-out and account deletion (`signOut()`), local persistence of authorization |\n| T3 trigger scan | none beyond T4 |\n| Bounded T1 | none |\n| Canonical builder | Claude Opus 5.5 (B-HC8-119 opening; B-HC9-119 fix round 1) |\n| Parent owner | operator agent 119; stack H1 #359 -> H2 #360 -> H3 #361 -> H4 #362 -> H5 #363 -> H6 #364 -> **H7 (this PR)** |\n| Acceptance evidence | OPENING: failing-before [37241679887](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-mobile/actions/runs/37241679887), passing-after [37241704846](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-mobile/actions/runs/37241704846). FIX ROUND 1: failing-before [37244032480](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-mobile/actions/runs/37244032480), passing-after [37244045034](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-mobile/actions/runs/37244045034). PR CI at the head |\n| Promotion triggers | any change to grant binding (AsyncStorage session or SecureStore authority), sign-out order or deletion flow; native/device acceptance stays with the owner-approved EAS build |\n\n**Stack position H7**, base `agent115/wear-split-6-retire-samsung` (#364 @ `1266038cd311f3dcfd8e472c04e3241a3061866b`). #362 is at 2,983 of its 3,000 ceiling, so this fix is a new piece (new-PR limit 1,500). Never merge alone: H1-H7 land as one.\n\n**Size:** 1,205 changed lines (1,191 additions, 14 deletions); 156 production lines in 2 files, 1,049 test lines in 5 files. Under the 1,500 new-PR limit.\n\n## What changes\n- **Sol B-362-8 (was C-362-14).** `src/services/health/onDeviceState.ts`: every stored Connect grant now carries the phone's consent session (`wearables_on_device_session`, a random nonce with nothing personal, kept outside the `wearables_on_device:` prefix). In the state chain, sign-out enumerates keys, then **replaces the session before any removal**; when the new value cannot be written it removes the stored one. Then it removes the prefix keys as before. `getLocalAuthorization` honours a grant only when its session equals the stored one, so a grant that a failed `getAllKeys` or `removeMany` leaves on disk stays void in this run and after a restart. Fail closed: an absent or unreadable session, or a grant with no session, authorizes nothing. The next Connect starts a new session when none is stored; a session read failure on Connect rejects the grant write. `retireOnDeviceState()` with no source also removes the session (everything the module wrote). Feature not on main, so no stored grants predate the binding.\n- **Sol B-362-9.** `src/services/authActions.ts`: `signOut` keeps its synchronous `stopOnDeviceHealthWork()` and the sign-out epoch bump, then runs the rest inside `try/finally { await healthStateRetired }` (it never rejects). The parallel clear no longer holds the health promise: its own `finally` awaits it, so a `clearUserCache`/`clearAllStorage` rejection never lets `logout` fire, or `signOut` settle, before the health drain. An earlier throw (for example identity drain) also settles only after it. Account deletion ends in the same `signOut()`.\n- **C-362-13 remainder (Sol) = C-362-15 (Opus), same lines.** A failed grant write restores the latest grant that reached disk (`authCommittedAt`), never another failed reservation.\n- **Sol B-369-1 (fix round 1; the B-362-8 remainder, was builder C-369-1).** `src/services/health/onDeviceState.ts`: every grant is also bound to a consent authority in **SecureStore** (`wearables_on_device_authority`, Keychain / Keystore, a random nonce), a different store from the AsyncStorage backing store that holds the grant, the session and the progress. `retireOnDeviceStateAtSignOut()` revokes the authority **at once** (before the chain waits for any native AsyncStorage operation in flight) and **again first thing in the chain** (a grant write in flight may have started a new one), before any AsyncStorage write; when the SecureStore delete fails it writes a new random value, which voids every grant as well. `getLocalAuthorization` honours a grant only when both its session and its authority match; an absent or unreadable authority, or a grant without one, authorizes nothing. It also returns null when a sign-out started while it was reading. Connect starts an authority when none is stored; a failed authority read or write rejects the grant write (no unbound grant). `retireOnDeviceState()` with no source revokes the authority too. So an outage of every AsyncStorage mutation at sign-out, or an app exit while sign-out waits behind a held native write, no longer revives the old grant after a restart. Same-session consent still survives a restart.\n\n## Tests (in this piece)\n- `src/services/__tests__/authActions.storageOutage.sol119g.test.ts`: Sol's H7 probe, byte-identical; it is Sol's H46F suite (`authActions.restartGrant.sol119f`, which it replaces) plus the AsyncStorage mutation-outage case, a pure addition.\n- `src/services/health/__tests__/onDeviceState.failedGrantChain.sol119f.test.ts`: Sol's narrow C-362-13 remainder suite, byte-identical.\n- `src/services/health/__tests__/onDeviceState.signOutDurable.test.ts` (10 cases): getAllKeys and removeMany failure plus restart; session write and removal both failing; a grant write in flight at a failed sign-out; persistence-positive and successful-clear controls; new Connect after a failed sign-out (now and after restart); unreadable or missing session and session-less grants fail closed; a session read failure on Connect.\n- `src/services/__tests__/authActions.healthDrainFinally.test.ts` (3 cases): rejection inside the parallel clear, rejection before it, no-rejection control; held native write, logout ordering.\n- `src/services/health/__tests__/onDeviceState.authorityStore.test.ts` (9 cases, fix round 1): every AsyncStorage mutation failing at sign-out plus restart; an app exit while sign-out waits behind a held native write; a grant write in flight that starts a new authority after the first revocation; a failed SecureStore delete; unreadable, missing and authority-less grants fail closed; an authority write failure on Connect; a sign-out during a grant read; same-consent restart and full-retirement control.\n\n## Residual (documented, not claimed fixed)\nThe AsyncStorage-only residual of the opening (B-369-1) is closed. An old grant can now come back after a restart only if, in the same sign-out, SecureStore rejects both the authority delete and the replacement write AND AsyncStorage rejects the session write, the session removal and the prefix removal: two separate OS stores failing together. In that case the token deletion in the same SecureStore has failed as well (see the follow-up on `secureStorage.removeItem` in the B-HC9-119 report).\n\n**Rounds**\n| Round | Head | Builder | Change | Comment |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| OPENING | `35717bfe0053a3e6075f821e5763fb7a80634d51` | B-HC8-119 | B-362-8, B-362-9, C-362-13 remainder; 845 lines | [OPENING](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-mobile/pull/369#issuecomment-5985418514) |\n| FIX ROUND 1 | `3252ec79cd9ab1f28165a1913d8ae3096b590d4a` | B-HC9-119 | Sol B-369-1 (SecureStore consent authority); 1,205 lines | [FIX ROUND 1](https://github.com/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-mobile/pull/369#issuecomment-5985690624) |\n\n","created_at":"2026-10-04T22:58:43Z","updated_at":"2026-10-04T23:42:37Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"ad8f950a04d3b0026728642600718c1b40caddb6","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-mobile/pulls/369/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BradleyGleavePortfolio/growth-project-mobile/pulls